// the mask is r(4+n): 0x60 is r9 and r10) and no others. One line each: {0xENTRY, 0xMASK},  // the proof
{0x102e99f0, 0x60},  // its two callers are the direct `bl`s of 0x102e4530 (no descriptor, no virtual slot) and read r9 and r10 (and the result r3) after the call: tools/register_contract.py --after 0x102e99f0; no routine of the block writes r9 or r10, so they are what the last callee left, as in the original
{0x102ea3c0, 0x60},  // its one caller is the direct `bl` of 0x102e4530 and reads r9, r10 and the result: tools/register_contract.py --after 0x102ea3c0; r9 and r10 are never written by the block
{0x102dc000, 0x60},  // its two callers are the direct `bl`s of 0x102e4530 and read r9 and r10 (the second ignores the result): tools/register_contract.py --after 0x102dc000; r9 and r10 are never written by the block
{0x102dcb20, 0x70},  // its one caller is the direct `bl` of 0x102d86c0 (no descriptor, no virtual slot) and reads r8-r10 (and the result r3) after the call: tools/register_contract.py --after 0x102dcb20 (they flow on into 0x102dee70); the routine writes none of them on a reachable path (only the scaled draw's arithmetic does), so they are what its last callee left, as in the original
{0x102dd910, 0x78},  // its one caller is the direct `bl` of 0x102d8830 and reads r7-r10 (and r3) after the call: tools/register_contract.py --after 0x102dd910; r7-r10 are written only in the unreachable scaled draw
{0x102de6e0, 0x78},  // its one caller is the direct `bl` of 0x102d86c0 and reads r7-r10 (and r3): tools/register_contract.py --after 0x102de6e0; r7-r10 are written only in the unreachable scaled draw
{0x102dc410, 0x78},  // its two callers are the direct `bl`s of 0x102dbf00, whose caller 0x102dabb0 is compared on r7-r10: the scaled forms' inline copies leave r7 (nation term) and r7, r8 (last term) as the original; r9 and r10 are never written
{0x102dbf00, 0x78},  // its one caller is the direct `bl` of 0x102dabb0, compared on r7-r10 (below): r7 and r8 are what the last score left, r9 and r10 pass through
{0x102dabb0, 0x78},  // compared on r7-r10; its one caller is the direct `bl` at 0x101198f0 (no descriptor, no virtual slot). The continuation: 0x103d0950 (reads r3, r4; writes r0, r4, r5, r6), 0x1013ae10 (reads r3; writes r0, r3), then either `li r3,0; bl 0x100cae30` (reads r3; writes r6-r8 on its r3 == 0 branch, passes r9 and r10 on) into qsort4x 0x10768300 (comparator TOC -0x7660 = 0x100cd390, reads r3, r4), or the daily scan 0x102d86c0 (which reads r7 and r8 through qsort4x's indirect call and 0x102de6e0 -> 0x10362d70 reads r8: .local/rewrites/player_regen/pending/leftover_flow.py), so r7-r10 are compared and the rewrite leaves them as the original: r7 = count - 1 after the removal of the pool entry (0x102deb70, set by the routine), r7/r8 from the last candidate score's scaled draw (0x102dc410, compared on them), r9/r10 pass through. r4-r6 are not compared: tools/register_contract.py --after and the flow tool (r4-r8, from 0x101198f4) find them written on every path (r4 by the caller, r5 and r6 by 0x103d0950).
